# Round 18, C1-15 (fixed). L §4.2: day_of "Of a key of an anchored index (§4.1) it is refused, and so is schedule, at
# load where load sees the index (§8.4), otherwise at the key (RUN-DOMAIN)"; L §8.3 LOAD-DOMAIN "<operation> has no
# meaning for <values> (§8.4, seen at load)". d's key binds over am, anchored on the 17th: load sees it, and the whole
# reality is refused. snap11: q RUN-DOMAIN at the key.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
index am = month 2026-01..2026-12 from 17
input dom: int
def d[k in am]: date = day_of(k, dom)
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  dom = 5
ask q: d[2026-03]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN day_of of a key of the anchored index am has no meaning (m.tally:9)
